## Also write the usage document

`doc/usage-{{ jira }}.md` is part of this phase, not a later one: what a change
looks like from outside is a design decision, and writing it here is what
catches a design that cannot be explained to its users.

Write it into the repository at that path as you work — it is committed with
the design. Cover setup, the commands a user runs, the user-visible behaviour,
rollout, operations, and support notes. If the change genuinely has no
user-visible surface, write the file containing `N/A` and the reason; an absent
file cannot be told from a forgotten one.
